{"availability":"available","full":"driftphp/demo","name":"demo","description":"Demo for DriftPHP","category":"Other","language":"CSS","stars":129,"forks":11,"created":"2019-11-21T18:49:15Z","updated":"2023-02-01T23:50:16Z","branch":"master","homepage":"https://driftphp.io","topics":["demo","driftphp","reactphp","redis"],"demo":"https://driftphp.io/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T11:08:03.994Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T11:08:03.994Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T11:08:03.994Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T11:08:03.994Z","stars":129,"forks":11}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Remember. This is a demo package. We encourage to make us PRs if you find some bugs, but we're not going to add new features unless is necessary.","This demo supports PHP8. We only made 2 changes to make this happen. First of all, new DriftPHP projects that want to change to PHP8 should start using the php8 Docker image - driftphp/base-php8 -. After that, and because some dependencies don't have their updates to accept the new PHP version, you should install/update your composer dependencies with the flag --ignore-platform-reqs. With these 2 changes, we want to welcome PHP8 with a big smile on our faces :)","This project is a sample for integrating Symfony and ReactPHP. The base of the project is a simple and clean DriftPHP installation using drift/skeleton, so that means that, if your code is built on top of that structure, you're a little bit nearer than turning your project non-blocking."],"features":["Command Bus + AMQP Adapter","Event Bus + AMQP Adapter","We want simplicity. No more Nginx for a simple server","We want performance. Each ms matters. Really.","We want a non-blocking implementation. If we have one long query, we don't"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/driftphp/demo/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"cb6583fd0b5820a84bfa85114bedbadd49a0ef3354eac77f3b237947062eff5d","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T11:08:04